TERMS OF SALE FOR COMMERCIAL LICENCES

These terms apply when you buy a Sluurp commercial licence (a "business
licence"). What a licence lets you do is set out above; these terms cover the
purchase itself. Last updated: 1 October 2026.

S1. Who you buy from

   You buy from Zeneka ("we", "us"). You are the person or
   business named on the order ("you"). By placing an order you accept these
   terms and the Sluurp License. If you buy for a business, you confirm that
   you may act for it. Business licences are sold to businesses and
   professionals; a private person using Sluurp for themselves, without
   earning money from it, needs no licence.

S2. What you buy

   A business licence is a key that allows commercial use of Sluurp on
   every server the business runs, swarm nodes included, paid once. Its
   price is the one shown at
   https://sluurp.org/business when you buy it, including any offer running
   then. A licence bought at an offer price is the same licence, and keeps
   working as any other.

   A licence is paid once and does not expire. It covers every version of
   Sluurp released while you hold it, for as long as Sluurp is offered under
   these terms. We may change what later versions include, or their prices,
   for new purchases; a licence you already hold keeps working.

S3. Prices and taxes

   Prices are in US dollars and do not include taxes. Where the law requires
   it, value added tax, sales tax or a similar tax is added at checkout,
   based on where you are. A business with a valid VAT or tax number may be
   charged no tax where the reverse-charge rules apply; you are then
   responsible for declaring it. Prices may change at any time; the price
   you pay is the one shown when you place the order.

S4. Payment

   Payment is taken in full when you order, by the methods offered at
   checkout. Card and bank details go straight to our payment provider; we
   never see or store them. Your licence key is sent once the payment has
   cleared.

S5. Invoices

   Each purchase comes with an invoice, sent by email to the address on the
   order, showing the business name, address and tax number you give at
   checkout, and any tax charged. If a detail is wrong, tell us within 30
   days and we will issue a corrected invoice.

S6. Refunds

   Ask for a refund within 30 days of the purchase and we give you your money
   back in full, with no questions asked, to the method you paid with. Once a
   licence is refunded, its key stops being valid, and any server using it
   commercially needs another licence. After 30 days, purchases are not
   refundable, except where the law says otherwise or where we cannot deliver
   what you bought.

S7. Support and updates

   Updates are published at https://github.com/SluurpHQ/releases, where bugs
   are reported and features asked for. Licence holders get answers about
   their licence and purchases by email. Sluurp is in alpha: we fix what we
   can, but we do not promise a response time or that a particular problem
   will be fixed.

S8. Liability

   As far as the law allows, our total liability for anything to do with a
   purchase is limited to what you paid for it. We are not liable for lost
   profits, lost data or indirect damages. Nothing in these terms limits
   liability that the law says cannot be limited.

S9. Ending a licence

   A licence ends if you break the Sluurp License or these terms, for example
   by passing a key on to another business. It also ends if a payment is
   reversed or charged back. When it ends, stop using Sluurp commercially on
   the servers it covered. No refund is due for a licence that ends because
   the terms were broken.

S10. Changes to these terms

   We may update these terms. The version in force when you buy applies to
   that purchase.

S11. Law and disputes

   These terms are governed by the law of the country where the Sluurp
   authors are established. Disputes go to its courts, unless the law of your
   country gives you the right to go to yours.

Questions about licensing or a purchase: https://sluurp.org/business
